[{"id":"VRCE-3-3-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":1,"english":"Then Virādha again spoke filling the forest, Do you tell me who ask you, who are you and whither are you going? The North-West Provinces text has additional Sloka : Having said this, the graceful Lakşmaņa spoke to Virādha as if jestingly, Who are you that coming to the forest, are ranging it pleasantly?-","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2cd2eb57d9b870a4d34cbfc5c2fd4bfd09e90ebf4dabf0faf5e50476649a5781","compact":"3f5b9b17e7d1a0aa2ce0f76a95cac1fe3ccfbf0e91069ba3c8f45f371574c11e","nasal":"3f5b9b17e7d1a0aa2ce0f76a95cac1fe3ccfbf0e91069ba3c8f45f371574c11e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":2,"english":"Thereupon, the highly energetic Rāma answered the Rākşasa with a flaming face, when he had thus asked (Rāma) that he belonged to the Iksvaku race. Know us that are in the forest, for Kșatriyas of respectable character. I also am anxious of knowing who you are, wandering in the Dandakas.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d7060fc425b2cb2a148fc5f17a241ce9fe59c706756519a81e8bc3f1bac4e625","compact":"32e5c27b64b972c58b0cf666bde541aaddc324e5dd51e8b2ff2e418a1fece9a2","nasal":"0b5522adadc6b4658618bb8072aff8eadab0fbb01b3b448760f6df203fdbed8b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":3,"english":"Thereupon, the highly energetic Rāma answered the Rākşasa with a flaming face, when he had thus asked (Rāma) that he belonged to the Iksvaku race. Know us that are in the forest, for Kșatriyas of respectable character. I also am anxious of knowing who you are, wandering in the Dandakas.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.783,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a1838b60ccf55f2763a0d69447e88f18c35dd7cf40faf925e49f8993c55c524f","compact":"8665319e2fb5e228732265e853a82740b0177bf0b29f302ca68d09e2385e1884","nasal":"42157900fdeacdfde10536c17055112d87ef8c973f5d9b1e0bfa22d2cbb2b731"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":4,"english":"Virădha answered Råma having truth for his prowess, Ah! I will tell you, O king. Do you,O Răghava understand!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"624234d3c63f77a9d0c310c4bb3c38726d1c382de2806e6728afce875608023d","compact":"a8091b3f2d4315075d3855ee527ec6f6bfaf7145e0feebe6861db1522367d296","nasal":"dc5a70a3007799b4161ebf9429e558a7ac6362a584cde7f6af26941eb28daee2"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":5,"english":"I am son of Java, and my mother is Satahradā. All the Rāksasas of the earth have called me Virādha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7051733efc85d6e0b977065f58c977191b6f10bfc7ed83c3e788ac6da2e11021","compact":"3426b769d4837315fcada6dc80e515beace38d0d8d3cceab5d54439fe46a9ad1","nasal":"3426b769d4837315fcada6dc80e515beace38d0d8d3cceab5d54439fe46a9ad1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":6,"english":"Having gratified Brahmă by my asceticism, IⓇreceived (this boon) that none in the world would be able to slay me by mangling my body with weapons.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.853,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"679b97f2936ebb55a1009287f0faebcff01caedd18db6e8d520fb2d668810d6f","compact":"9b6d0a7160240a9343446c337b6adf2142607697790b02b2cd709bb3fdff64cb","nasal":"9b6d0a7160240a9343446c337b6adf2142607697790b02b2cd709bb3fdff64cb"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":7,"english":"Forsaking this fair one, do you, renouncing all hope (of either recovering her or vanquishing me), speedily flee away to that place whence you had come; else I shall deprive you of your lives. Thereat, Rāma with his eyes reddened through wrath replied to that Rākşasa of a deformed shape, the wicked Viradha.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b997f88c05f42576727956714d3ac51cae45f0892385f6336f2d3ad6364afa6b","compact":"7bc3ea3f46ff882a523906d27bed758245456b1fdc4e09693bd2dddf1455b3fd","nasal":"7bc3ea3f46ff882a523906d27bed758245456b1fdc4e09693bd2dddf1455b3fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":8,"english":"Forsaking this fair one, do you, renouncing all hope (of either recovering her or vanquishing me), speedily flee away to that place whence you had come; else I shall deprive you of your lives. Thereat, Rāma with his eyes reddened through wrath replied to that Rākşasa of a deformed shape, the wicked Viradha.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.982,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0e7ce05d82d87b24342b9d9ffea0b76302ae4630ccf6c7f66ff7b8094126bf6b","compact":"b52e21f82013b4d4e4cf91740a4c015d6160bc440b163a26ab7e2eadfab430d1","nasal":"b52e21f82013b4d4e4cf91740a4c015d6160bc440b163a26ab7e2eadfab430d1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":9,"english":"Little! shame on you of base purposes! You surely seek your own death; and (death) you shall get in battle. Stay! You escapist me not with life.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.675,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"604aa4014500301a28df352a53b7e744e694e2a087202527903745de8ad77850","compact":"e69789e25829a56c37f1a8299fb3ef1fbccf2347d90865544abf3f03cb4c65bb","nasal":"e69789e25829a56c37f1a8299fb3ef1fbccf2347d90865544abf3f03cb4c65bb"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":10,"english":"Then stringing his bow, Rāma, speedily aiming at the Rākşasa, pierced him with sharpened shafts; and (then) from his bow-string let go seven shafts, having their feathered parts plaited with good, furnished with great velocity, and coursing like Suparna or the wind.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.847,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4fcc2c04c5f156cdf69ec6ba9d65b4d4d300fc4eb8f062860efce32ef0e757c","compact":"1759f502a5ccee41fc8b25d9c55bdc4e9f4fa9d22f9124011ce56c339e274bce","nasal":"1759f502a5ccee41fc8b25d9c55bdc4e9f4fa9d22f9124011ce56c339e274bce"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":11,"english":"Then stringing his bow, Rāma, speedily aiming at the Rākşasa, pierced him with sharpened shafts; and (then) from his bow-string let go seven shafts, having their feathered parts plaited with good, furnished with great velocity, and coursing like Suparna or the wind.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d2319dface80d422bd148e65fe729373750de27b002f865913eb4e9c975cc275","compact":"9058b0ee4b8a3f3a545f0ee4d0169c45f2ed94d44e478303ed89435cf80f4dd3","nasal":"89ab71468454a55ba4e0924f0dcaa9289e6ae16c515592baf3748ec746bb6d67"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":12,"english":"Thereat, resembling flames, those arrows furnished with peacocks, feathers, pierced. Viradha's body, and fell to the earth, covered with blood.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8bb0b8bbc13e5525c9cc3fc54e97518ddb906cb5f302c7cf2f0e5196de262df7","compact":"1837e534632e9f523ffb48a32d6561e2102cce86834fdb8b4ea88d9b8856710e","nasal":"1837e534632e9f523ffb48a32d6561e2102cce86834fdb8b4ea88d9b8856710e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-3-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":3,"verse":13,"english":"And sending forth a mighty roar, he took up a dart resembling the banner of Sakra and he then appeared like the Destroyer* with opening mouth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-3-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3003013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"58231b829a9f329fee28a35d7d7a